!! What it does

OKF (Open Knowledge Format, v0.2) describes a knowledge base as a folder of markdown files — one ''concept'' per file, its metadata in YAML frontmatter, its ID being the file path. This plugin lets TiddlyWiki read and write such folders: every concept is a tiddler, every save produces a valid OKF document, and keys TiddlyWiki doesn't know survive the round-trip.

It doesn't patch TiddlyWiki itself. It registers on the three extension hooks of `rimir/frontmatter`, which still does the file detection and saving.

!! How it works

```
---
type: Metric
title: Monthly Revenue
tags: [finance, revenue]
generated: { by: agent/x, at: 2026-06-20T22:53:05Z }
---
# Revenue
```

in `tiddlers/metrics/revenue.md` loads as

|!Field |!Value |
|`title` |`metrics/revenue` (from the path) |
|`type` |`text/markdown` |
|`okf.type` |`Metric` |
|`caption` |`Monthly Revenue` |
|`tags` |`finance revenue` |
|`okf.generated` |`{"by":"agent/x","at":"2026-06-20T22:53:05Z"}` |

and is written back to the same file.

!! Which files are OKF

# A file whose YAML `type` is not a TiddlyWiki content type (`Metric`, `Playbook`, …) — ''always'' (safety rule)
# Otherwise: tiddlers matching the scope filter (Settings); an empty filter means ''every'' frontmatter `.md`

Everything else is left to plain `rimir/frontmatter`.

!! Key design decisions

* ''Separate plugin, hooks in frontmatter'' — frontmatter stays small and flat; OKF brings its own YAML parser (js-yaml) and mapping
* ''`type` belongs to OKF'' — the concept type lives in `okf.type`; the TW type is implied (`text/markdown`) and never written
* ''`title` is a display name'' — OKF `title` ↔ `caption`; the tiddler title comes from the path, or from `tw.title` when the path can't express it
* ''Path = concept ID'' — existing files are never moved; new concepts go to `<title>.md` with folders
* ''Old frontmatter files stay readable'' — no `type` and no `tw.title` means "written by frontmatter": its `title` is the tiddler title
* ''Default type `tiddler`'' — OKF requires a `type`; tiddlers without `okf.type` get the configurable default, which is not materialised as a field on load

